+
+#### [Pipecat Flows](https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat-flows)
+> **Description:** Pipecat Flows is described as an open source conversation framework for structured Pipecat dialogues, which is useful when voice systems need deterministic business steps rather than free-form chat alone. Restaurants often need exactly that for order capture, modifier confirmation, allergy questions, and payment or pickup instructions. GitHub lists the repo as BSD-2-Clause licensed, primarily Python, with 520 stars and a last commit date of Dec 22, 2025. It works best as the layer that keeps a voice experience operationally safe while still leveraging the broader Pipecat ecosystem.
+
