+
+#### [Vocode Core](https://github.com/vocodedev/vocode-core)
+> **Description:** Vocode presents itself as an open source library for voice-based LLM apps, with abstractions for phone calls, Zoom, transcription services, synthesis services, and model integrations. That is directly relevant to restaurants experimenting with inbound call automation, call deflection for FAQs, or outbound reminder calls. GitHub shows it as MIT licensed, primarily Python, with 3,644 stars and a last commit date of Nov 16, 2024. The project is useful when the goal is a modular voice stack that can mix open components with telephony infrastructure while still remaining code-centric and self-managed.
+
