+> **Description:** Bolna is an open source orchestration framework for production-ready conversational voice AI agents. Its README is explicit that the repository covers the orchestration layer used to combine ASR, LLM, and TTS providers over websockets, which is exactly the kind of stack a restaurant needs for voice ordering prototypes. GitHub lists the repo as MIT licensed, mainly Python, with 487 stars and a last commit date of Nov 18, 2025. It is best suited to teams that want to own the orchestration logic while swapping models and providers as voice quality or latency requirements change.
