+## Why This List
+Open source matters for restaurants because margins are tight, workflows are operationally messy, and vendor lock-in is expensive. The best AI tools for restaurants 2026 are not only about flashy chat interfaces; they are about owning your data, self-hosting where needed, integrating with existing ordering or POS systems, and adapting models to local menus, hours, languages, and operational constraints. This list only includes public GitHub repositories and excludes proprietary SaaS-only products.
