+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for restaurants in 2026?
+For most teams, the strongest starting stack is `Rasa` or `Botpress` for guest-facing chat, `Pipecat` or `Vocode` for voice experiences, `EasyOCR` or `Unstructured` for menu and document ingestion, and `NeuralForecast` or `Darts` for demand forecasting.
+
+### Are there truly restaurant-specific open source AI repositories on GitHub?
+Very few. The honest answer is that most public repos are horizontal AI tools, not restaurant-native products. That is why this list maps general open source AI projects to restaurant workflows instead of pretending there are dozens of restaurant-only repositories.
+
+### Which open source AI repos are best for restaurant phone ordering?
+`Pipecat`, `Pipecat Flows`, `Vocode Core`, `Bolna`, `Whisper`, `Coqui TTS`, and `Piper` are the best current building blocks. They cover real-time voice orchestration, speech recognition, and speech synthesis.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for menu OCR and invoice extraction?
+`EasyOCR`, `Unstructured`, `Layout Parser`, and `LiteParse` are the cleanest fits in this list. They are not restaurant-native, but they are strong for turning menus, invoices, and SOPs into structured data or searchable content.
+
+### What open source AI tools help restaurants forecast demand and staffing?
+`NeuralForecast`, `Darts`, `PyTorch Forecasting`, and `MLForecast` are the best options here. They can be adapted for hourly sales, item demand, prep volume, labor planning, and anomaly detection.
+
+### Can I self-host these AI tools for restaurants?
+Many of them, yes. This list prioritizes repositories that can be run or adapted from public GitHub code, and several are explicitly self-hosted or local-first, including `Tiledesk`, `Open WebUI`, `Flowise`, `Piper`, and parts of the voice stack.
+
+### What is missing from the open source restaurant AI ecosystem?
+The biggest gaps are POS-native AI copilots, reservation-specific AI frameworks, table management AI, kitchen throughput optimization tools, and restaurant-focused model evaluation suites. Those remain opportunities for new open source projects.
+
+## GitHub Search Queries Used
+
+Direct restaurant-only searches returned almost no useful public repos, so the research expanded into adjacent categories that restaurants can adapt:
+
