+#### [EasyOCR](https://github.com/JaidedAI/EasyOCR)
+> **Description:** EasyOCR is a ready-to-use OCR library with support for 80+ languages and many writing systems, and the README focuses on straightforward deployment rather than a heavy document pipeline. For restaurants, that makes it useful for digitizing menus, scanning printed supplier documents, or extracting text from table cards and signage when a lightweight OCR layer is enough. GitHub shows it as Apache-2.0 licensed, primarily Python, with 28,544 stars and a last commit date of Dec 5, 2025. It is usually the fastest path to a working OCR baseline before investing in more advanced parsing stacks.
