+### Demand Forecasting and Operations Planning
+
+Gap note: open source demand forecasting is mature, but restaurant-specific repositories for prep sheets, waste optimization, or labor planning are still scarce. Most teams will adapt general time-series libraries.
+
+#### [NeuralForecast](https://github.com/Nixtla/neuralforecast)
+> **Description:** NeuralForecast offers a large collection of state-of-the-art neural forecasting models ranging from RNNs to transformers, with support for exogenous variables, probabilistic outputs, and familiar fit and predict workflows. Restaurants can use it for sales forecasting, item-level demand, staffing estimation, and prep planning when weather, holidays, promotions, and local events matter. GitHub shows it as Apache-2.0 licensed, primarily Python, with 3,923 stars and a last commit date of Jan 14, 2026. It is one of the strongest open choices when restaurants need modern forecasting models rather than classical baselines alone.
