+## TL;DR
+- `RasaHQ/rasa`, `botpress/botpress`, and `theopenconversationkit/tock` are the strongest open source foundations for restaurant chat, reservations, FAQs, and guest-service automations.
+- `pipecat-ai/pipecat`, `vocodedev/vocode-core`, `openai/whisper`, `coqui-ai/TTS`, and `rhasspy/piper` are the most practical starting stack for voice ordering and phone automation.
+- `JaidedAI/EasyOCR`, `Unstructured-IO/unstructured`, `Layout-Parser/layout-parser`, and `run-llama/liteparse` are the clearest fits for menu ingestion, invoice parsing, and document-heavy back office workflows.
+- `Nixtla/neuralforecast`, `unit8co/darts`, `sktime/pytorch-forecasting`, and `Nixtla/mlforecast` are the best open source choices for demand forecasting, prep planning, and labor scheduling models.
+- There is still a major open source gap in restaurant-native POS copilot, table management AI, and kitchen AI products; where that gap exists, this README says so directly.
